{"id": "q103", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["1910.10683:0049", "1910.10683:0048", "2007.01282:0010", "2004.04906:0047", "1910.10683:0053", "2112.04426:0068", "1910.10683:0041", "2112.04426:0012"], "text": "I couldn't find sufficient evidence in the available sources.", "abstained": true, "cited": [], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_86dc843b12", "input_tokens": 2643, "output_tokens": 50, "reasoning_tokens": 31, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "8544d7cfef87c1719d0fad99291af291eed52136f79d1e9b172cdcea80a39cd6", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 8.86279996484518, "dense": 10395.64669993706, "fusion": 0.13649999164044857, "generation": 1152.9014999978244}, "wait_ms": 0.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q104", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2005.11401:0006", "2005.11401:0007", "2005.11401:0008", "2005.11401:0021", "2005.11401:0030", "2005.11401:0023", "2005.11401:0038", "2005.11401:0026"], "text": "The RAG‑Sequence variant treats the retrieved passage as a single latent document that is used for generating the entire output sequence; the same document conditions every token of the answer and the sequence probability is obtained by marginalising over the top‑K documents as a whole [2]. In contrast, the RAG‑Token variant allows a separate latent document to be drawn for each target token, marginalising over the top‑K documents independently at every step so that different tokens can draw content from different passages [3].", "abstained": false, "cited": [2, 3], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_5e2577217c", "input_tokens": 2465, "output_tokens": 153, "reasoning_tokens": 40, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "1b9f785ca39ccaebf643efdcce6d97740c35d2c42f97cca53ec127b8b1f6e35c", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 10.437099961563945, "dense": 23.9245998673141, "fusion": 0.09169988334178925, "generation": 714.638700010255}, "wait_ms": 0.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q105", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2307.03172:0015", "2307.03172:0007", "2307.03172:0045", "2307.03172:0044", "2307.03172:0043", "2307.03172:0020", "2307.03172:0014", "2307.03172:0036"], "text": "When the answer appears in the middle of a long retrieved set, GPT‑3.5‑Turbo’s accuracy drops dramatically. With 20 retrieved documents, its score falls to about 50 percent when the relevant passage is at index 9 (the middle position) [4], and with 30 retrieved documents it falls to roughly 50 percent at index 9 as well [3]. By contrast, in the closed‑book setting—where the model must rely only on its parametric memory—the same model achieves 56.1 percent accuracy [1].", "abstained": false, "cited": [4, 3, 1], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_5e2577217c", "input_tokens": 2514, "output_tokens": 194, "reasoning_tokens": 65, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "47358d2baee004d64212f670fbb3196706d85d7a379fa83f84d062e5abb2ebc0", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 12.305399868637323, "dense": 27.358300052583218, "fusion": 0.08570007048547268, "generation": 902.2172999102622}, "wait_ms": 59365.99999982864, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q112", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2004.12832:0032", "2004.12832:0017", "2004.12832:0016", "2004.12832:0044", "2004.12832:0020", "2004.12832:0014", "2004.12832:0031", "2004.12832:0021"], "text": "ColBERT represents each token with a fixed‑size embedding of \\(m\\) dimensions, and in the experiments the authors set this dimension to 128 [7].", "abstained": false, "cited": [7], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_4200b3f836", "input_tokens": 3426, "output_tokens": 102, "reasoning_tokens": 57, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "876eb46d4ab55bc850ee5caf97fd36c017ed34540469cf93050a973678553421", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 5.899199983105063, "dense": 23.13639991916716, "fusion": 0.12370012700557709, "generation": 695.0201999861747}, "wait_ms": 60084.00000017136, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q113", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2104.08663:0026", "2104.08663:0033", "2104.08663:0022", "2104.08663:0018", "2104.08663:0000", "2104.08663:0003", "2104.08663:0025", "2104.08663:0027"], "text": "The cross‑attentional re‑ranking model (BM25 + cross‑encoder) beats plain BM25 on most of the BEIR zero‑shot datasets—specifically, it outperforms BM25 on 16 of the 18 datasets evaluated. It falls short on the two tasks that are most dissimilar from the MS MARCO training data, ArguAna and Touché‑2020, where it does not surpass BM25【1】.", "abstained": false, "cited": [1], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_fe269835c7", "input_tokens": 3175, "output_tokens": 164, "reasoning_tokens": 59, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "eaa2fe412f080d46c91945002503619e8e0ad49d12ebdceed556cb6a736955b9", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 14.403499895706773, "dense": 27.757899835705757, "fusion": 0.11570006608963013, "generation": 770.807099994272}, "wait_ms": 60084.999999869615, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q115", "type": "unanswerable", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2109.01652:0026", "2203.15556:0042", "2112.04426:0059", "2003.10555:0020", "2206.07682:0048", "2203.15556:0003", "2112.04426:0069", "2112.04426:0040"], "text": "I couldn't find sufficient evidence in the available sources.", "abstained": true, "cited": [], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_5a93aea882", "input_tokens": 3095, "output_tokens": 46, "reasoning_tokens": 27, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "126cf6067d96dde684c1c7fe3d3d2fd5ce06478ab45a6338fe1cb1aaa147d242", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 7.754800142720342, "dense": 19.495299784466624, "fusion": 0.09119999594986439, "generation": 735.185399884358}, "wait_ms": 60100.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q201", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["1910.10683:0030", "1910.10683:0009", "1706.03762:0000", "1409.0473:0014", "2112.04426:0026", "1706.03762:0035", "1910.10683:0130", "1409.0473:0025"], "text": "The model used a shortlist of 30 000 of the most frequent words for each language [4] and any word not in that shortlist was replaced with a special unknown token [UNK] [4].", "abstained": false, "cited": [4], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_86dc843b12", "input_tokens": 2683, "output_tokens": 113, "reasoning_tokens": 60, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "af1c528294188f8049235a064199a8202f4ae02d36eb9070893d0a56592ba38f", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 12.58770003914833, "dense": 25.89489985257387, "fusion": 0.1314000692218542, "generation": 1726.80880012922}, "wait_ms": 60100.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q203", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["1910.10683:0011", "2104.09864:0000", "2104.09864:0004", "2104.09864:0015", "2104.09864:0006", "2104.09864:0026", "2104.09864:0005", "2104.09864:0014"], "text": "Rotary Position Embedding (RoPE) makes the attention score between two tokens decrease as their relative distance grows, i.e., the inter‑token dependency decays with increasing offset [2][3]. This behavior is caused by the RoPE mechanism itself, which encodes positions by multiplying the token representations with a rotation matrix that inherently incorporates relative‑position information and yields a distance‑dependent decay [2][3].", "abstained": false, "cited": [2, 3], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_f73454f048", "input_tokens": 2569, "output_tokens": 153, "reasoning_tokens": 58, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "62d13c4fd50d4abf6bc8eb985d6b600c29f4bb69b5b4aada36250d610331c0ec", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 10.867299977689981, "dense": 22.20670017413795, "fusion": 0.0887999776750803, "generation": 871.006399858743}, "wait_ms": 0.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q207", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2302.04761:0058", "2106.09685:0064", "2106.09685:0066", "2001.08361:0038", "2203.02155:0038", "1907.11692:0028", "2106.09685:0065", "2005.14165:0015"], "text": "I couldn't find sufficient evidence in the available sources.", "abstained": true, "cited": [], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_c15aa9c1b7", "input_tokens": 2869, "output_tokens": 57, "reasoning_tokens": 38, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "f1733a71ae6a34095cb19f84435377449dcc4bd18ec1354d21f9987f233a9842", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 5.933000007644296, "dense": 21.80769992992282, "fusion": 0.09460002183914185, "generation": 960.6874999590218}, "wait_ms": 59225.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q208", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["1907.11692:0021", "1907.11692:0009", "1810.04805:0060", "1810.04805:0059", "2003.10555:0000", "1810.04805:0015", "1810.04805:0041", "1907.11692:0013"], "text": "RoBERTa notes that the original BERT code applied masking only once during preprocessing, which would give a static mask for a sentence across epochs. To prevent the exact same mask from being used in every epoch, the training data were duplicated ten times so that each sequence could be presented with ten different masking patterns over the course of training [1]. Because the model was trained for 40 epochs, each particular mask still appeared multiple times: each sequence was seen with the same mask about four times during training [1].", "abstained": false, "cited": [1], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_5a93aea882", "input_tokens": 2535, "output_tokens": 164, "reasoning_tokens": 49, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "56cfd25dfa7a94fc6a1b055dde5d17ec86b6f19c87fe218a441b2a4695793caa", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 11.282500112429261, "dense": 27.35029999166727, "fusion": 0.09030010551214218, "generation": 1460.5642999522388}, "wait_ms": 0.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q212", "type": "comparison", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2104.09864:0000", "2104.09864:0019", "2104.09864:0064", "2104.09864:0004", "2104.09864:0006", "2104.09864:0051", "2104.09864:0069", "2104.09864:0067"], "text": "The original Transformer supplies word‑order information by adding an explicit absolute‑position embedding to each token’s representation before the self‑attention layers, so that the queries and keys carry a fixed positional signal for each position in the sequence【5】.  \n\nRoFormer replaces that additive scheme with Rotary Position Embedding (RoPE), which encodes each token’s absolute position as a rotation matrix applied to its query and key vectors and simultaneously injects relative‑position dependence directly into the inner‑product of queries and keys in the self‑attention computation【1】【4】. This rotation‑based encoding provides the model with both absolute and relative order cues without simply adding a separate positional vector.", "abstained": false, "cited": [5, 1, 4], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_dee443f41b", "input_tokens": 2331, "output_tokens": 208, "reasoning_tokens": 62, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "5288488c84bada354cb05ac9d58da41279da1eaaed5aca66c7d93852d12a3a2e", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 7.430800003930926, "dense": 23.593800142407417, "fusion": 0.08730008266866207, "generation": 942.8268999326974}, "wait_ms": 58630.99999995902, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q213", "type": "comparison", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["1910.10683:0013", "2005.14165:0110", "1910.10683:0007", "1910.10683:0014", "2005.14165:0018", "1910.10683:0126", "1910.10683:0015", "1910.10683:0068"], "text": "The “Colossal Clean Crawled Corpus” (C4) that T5 uses is about 750 GB of text after the cleaning heuristics are applied【7】. The passages do not provide any information about the size of the filtered Common Crawl dataset that was used to train GPT‑3, so that comparison cannot be made from the available sources.", "abstained": false, "cited": [7], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_90620edd96", "input_tokens": 3005, "output_tokens": 134, "reasoning_tokens": 53, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "9ccc4ec6d4510dbe0f55d632fec60be4e2c4bce2e4b6c8c7e538a569484e69ab", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 9.093199856579304, "dense": 21.982899866998196, "fusion": 0.12159999459981918, "generation": 1123.8657999783754}, "wait_ms": 60075.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q216", "type": "unanswerable", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["1910.10683:0040", "2104.09864:0060", "1706.03762:0003", "1706.03762:0032", "1706.03762:0002", "1910.10683:0042", "1706.03762:0009", "1706.03762:0036"], "text": "I couldn't find sufficient evidence in the available sources.", "abstained": true, "cited": [], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_69334c0be3", "input_tokens": 2552, "output_tokens": 34, "reasoning_tokens": 15, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "4839261fc4ec4b2ea60f367592c38fc67b8ccdecbc28ef4eab7a0c3e6732d04d", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 7.542199920862913, "dense": 24.209900060668588, "fusion": 0.09949994273483753, "generation": 680.719800060615}, "wait_ms": 60100.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q301", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2203.15556:0008", "2203.15556:0058", "2203.15556:0059", "2203.15556:0007", "2104.09864:0015", "2104.09864:0014", "2203.15556:0056", "2001.08361:0043"], "text": "I couldn't find sufficient evidence in the available sources.", "abstained": true, "cited": [], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_4727af4560", "input_tokens": 2530, "output_tokens": 51, "reasoning_tokens": 32, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "e257462ae00305647e131c0d6145880986b0732716ef46e0bb2ef92babf3bc81", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 8.157000178471208, "dense": 24.14280013181269, "fusion": 0.09380001574754715, "generation": 695.1188000384718}, "wait_ms": 0.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q302", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2206.07682:0040", "2206.07682:0044", "2206.07682:0042", "2206.07682:0038", "2206.07682:0039", "2206.07682:0019", "2206.07682:0037", "2206.07682:0041"], "text": "No. Even when accuracy (or other downstream metrics) remains near‑random for small models, the log‑likelihood of the target (as measured by cross‑entropy loss) continues to improve as model size grows. The authors observe that cross‑entropy loss decreases for both correct and incorrect responses on emergent classification tasks and that loss improves for small‑scale models despite error rates staying at chance levels【1†L1-L4】【5†L1-L4】【7†L4-L7】.", "abstained": false, "cited": [1, 5, 7], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_8ea50c0161", "input_tokens": 2624, "output_tokens": 168, "reasoning_tokens": 55, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "b25d056a1b90393b8b6482e68b3eba60cd567f12a2841e82560a82880ee721a3", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 10.684499982744455, "dense": 24.64519999921322, "fusion": 0.13519986532628536, "generation": 772.7560999337584}, "wait_ms": 59397.00000002049, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q303", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["1706.03741:0012", "1706.03741:0025", "2009.01325:0055", "2305.18290:0085", "2009.01325:0011", "1706.03741:0039", "1706.03741:0040", "2305.18290:0068"], "text": "When a human judge marks the two trajectory clips as equally good, the recorded distribution μ is set to be uniform over the two options [1]. If the judge indicates that the clips are incomparable, that comparison is omitted entirely from the database [1].", "abstained": false, "cited": [1], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_e5b4e54fbb", "input_tokens": 2528, "output_tokens": 87, "reasoning_tokens": 25, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "0f79ab59107a8cdf4e2621251b9e86bb1af8a57d8644f7908896f99d182f37a8", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 10.394300101324916, "dense": 24.498000042513013, "fusion": 0.09670015424489975, "generation": 704.0697000920773}, "wait_ms": 0.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q304", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2009.01325:0006", "2009.01325:0021", "2009.01325:0016", "2305.18290:0029", "2009.01325:0000", "2009.01325:0002", "2009.01325:0005", "2009.01325:0051"], "text": "When the policy was optimized more aggressively against the learned reward model, its performance initially improved according to human labelers, but after a point further optimization caused the reward model’s predictions to diverge from true human preferences, eventually becoming anti‑correlated and producing worse summaries than before【2】.", "abstained": false, "cited": [2], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_90620edd96", "input_tokens": 3366, "output_tokens": 92, "reasoning_tokens": 24, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "561346359bd689aa76abf70a72dca3cd0eac5a1b61459777f029e2a0259c4ddf", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 7.335199974477291, "dense": 24.644599994644523, "fusion": 0.0917001161724329, "generation": 1764.6097999531776}, "wait_ms": 60090.99999982864, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q306", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2203.02155:0120", "2203.02155:0041", "2203.02155:0010", "2203.02155:0036", "2203.02155:0032", "2203.02155:0000", "2203.02155:0012", "2203.02155:0119"], "text": "The authors incorporated a pretraining‑loss term (the “pretraining mix” coefficient γ) into the PPO objective, mixing the RL reward with the original supervised loss during fine‑tuning. This additional pretraining loss helps recover the regressions on public NLP benchmarks such as DROP and SQuAD that otherwise appear when training only with the RL reward [8][1].", "abstained": false, "cited": [8, 1], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_d577f40f11", "input_tokens": 2685, "output_tokens": 113, "reasoning_tokens": 26, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "05f1181bd3ec2aefb0dbf3d4930fec4a49592af965df54eafe5ff835c100bd99", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 8.222099859267473, "dense": 27.456399984657764, "fusion": 0.09380001574754715, "generation": 643.267200095579}, "wait_ms": 60100.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q310", "type": "comparison", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2203.15556:0025", "2203.15556:0043", "2203.15556:0027", "2203.15556:0044", "2203.15556:0003", "2203.15556:0007", "2203.15556:0005", "2203.15556:0011"], "text": "Kaplan et al. (2020) argue that when compute is increased the model should grow much faster than the data, recommending roughly a 5.5‑fold increase in parameters while the number of training tokens is raised only about 1.8‑fold [5].  \n\nThe Chinchilla analysis reaches the opposite conclusion: it finds that the optimal allocation of a larger compute budget is to scale model size and training tokens in roughly equal proportion, training a model that is about four times smaller than Gopher but using about four times more tokens, and generally increasing parameters and data together rather than favoring one over the other [5][7][8].", "abstained": false, "cited": [5, 7, 8], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_27194a498a", "input_tokens": 2916, "output_tokens": 209, "reasoning_tokens": 63, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "1e4414f28d8521b15d3dc3b9bdba49635f23c7d061f070c6cd40b5ba446a245f", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 12.304800096899271, "dense": 24.10880010575056, "fusion": 0.0871000811457634, "generation": 1139.4321999978274}, "wait_ms": 60100.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q312", "type": "comparison", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2212.08073:0025", "2212.08073:0033", "2212.08073:0000", "2212.08073:0010", "2212.08073:0041", "2212.08073:0011", "2212.08073:0034", "2212.08073:0040"], "text": "In InstructGPT the preference labels are supplied by humans — human feedback is used to create the comparison data that is distilled into a preference model [1]. In Constitutional AI, the harmlessness preference labels are generated by the language model itself (AI feedback) while the helpfulness labels still come from humans [4].", "abstained": false, "cited": [1, 4], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_bb691ea66b", "input_tokens": 2457, "output_tokens": 109, "reasoning_tokens": 33, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "176e669317c02b7c6c508168d8d74b9f080106b96fad0844978ce7e043fb1418", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 6.95309997536242, "dense": 23.535599932074547, "fusion": 0.13800011947751045, "generation": 1243.854499887675}, "wait_ms": 60100.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
