{"id": "q316", "type": "unanswerable", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2305.18290:0085", "2305.18290:0035", "2305.18290:0034", "2305.18290:0038", "2501.12948:0081", "2305.18290:0033", "2203.02155:0125", "2205.14135:0107"], "text": "I couldn't find sufficient evidence in the available sources.", "abstained": true, "cited": [], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_f73454f048", "input_tokens": 2874, "output_tokens": 38, "reasoning_tokens": 19, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "1fe13d8c63577b41f5f5ec6ce9a42d5cb5cf4ca081ccce3b4ad96444af80a48e", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 7.329600164666772, "dense": 23.51159998215735, "fusion": 0.12589991092681885, "generation": 1088.5470998473465}, "wait_ms": 59522.00000002049, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q403", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2106.09685:0018", "2106.09685:0044", "2106.09685:0016", "2106.09685:0025", "2106.09685:0043", "2106.09685:0004", "2106.09685:0045", "2106.09685:0019"], "text": "LoRA achieved the highest downstream performance when it adapted the query and value projection matrices together ( \\(W_{q}\\) and \\(W_{v}\\) ) rather than any single attention weight or other combinations, given the same budget of trainable parameters [2][7].", "abstained": false, "cited": [2, 7], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_c800245357", "input_tokens": 2906, "output_tokens": 94, "reasoning_tokens": 25, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "1645987747d5c3b2e8e7ff55a008496ccfa9c7687884814b5334daca0eca017d", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 10.490900138393044, "dense": 20.008600084111094, "fusion": 0.08629984222352505, "generation": 597.5194000639021}, "wait_ms": 0.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q405", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2104.08821:0012", "2104.08821:0013", "2104.08821:0003", "2104.08821:0014", "2104.08821:0004", "2104.08821:0011", "2104.08821:0010", "2104.08821:0000"], "text": "In unsupervised SimCSE, using dropout to create the positive pair is more effective than editing the sentence itself.  Experiments that replace dropout with a “delete‑one‑word” augmentation achieve lower STS‑B scores (75.9 vs 82.5) and also obtain poorer uniformity–alignment trade‑offs, so the edited‑sentence pair does not outperform the dropout‑generated pair [1][6][2].", "abstained": false, "cited": [1, 6, 2], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_96d96a151c", "input_tokens": 3049, "output_tokens": 142, "reasoning_tokens": 42, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "236681525dcf8e5b04e2feb3b2c92cb3180ff873584ab72f99bfa8499afbbe49", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 9.92039986886084, "dense": 28.628700179979205, "fusion": 0.09019998833537102, "generation": 760.3854998014867}, "wait_ms": 60091.00000006147, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q407", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2309.07597:0025", "2212.03533:0027", "2309.07597:0035", "2309.07597:0036", "2309.07597:0026", "2212.03533:0030", "2004.04906:0013", "2004.04906:0023"], "text": "In BGE’s general‑purpose contrastive fine‑tuning the model relies solely on **in‑batch negative samples** rather than mining hard negatives, and it uses a **very large batch size (up to 19,200 examples)** to provide many such negatives and improve embedding discriminativeness【1†L1-L4】【5†L1-L3】.", "abstained": false, "cited": [1, 5], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_bb691ea66b", "input_tokens": 3131, "output_tokens": 123, "reasoning_tokens": 38, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "51429263d0a11f27c76bdd705ec86aa7c6835f2ff17614d0834442c62a1392e8", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 8.87180003337562, "dense": 28.555599972605705, "fusion": 0.09269989095628262, "generation": 894.8967999313027}, "wait_ms": 60100.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q411", "type": "comparison", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2104.08821:0033", "2104.08821:0041", "2104.08821:0003", "2104.08821:0002", "2104.08821:0015", "2104.08821:0000", "2104.08821:0004", "2104.08821:0031"], "text": "Supervised SimCSE incorporates NLI data by taking the entailment (premise‑hypothesis) pairs directly as positive examples in its contrastive loss and using the contradiction pairs (along with other in‑batch sentences) as hard negatives [3][4][5]. The paper does not describe how Sentence‑BERT utilizes NLI data, so that part of the comparison cannot be answered from the provided sources.", "abstained": false, "cited": [3, 4, 5], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_c800245357", "input_tokens": 2332, "output_tokens": 149, "reasoning_tokens": 55, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "f1ca305a6a9e820d2fe19415eceb198483b2017a50283d24aaeb25218cd79a99", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 7.320699980482459, "dense": 25.46480018645525, "fusion": 0.08919998072087765, "generation": 690.160300116986}, "wait_ms": 0.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q412", "type": "comparison", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2309.07597:0036", "2212.03533:0000", "2005.11401:0009", "2004.12832:0017", "2004.12832:0016", "2005.11401:0011", "2212.03533:0002", "2212.03533:0036"], "text": "I couldn't find sufficient evidence in the available sources.", "abstained": true, "cited": [], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_c800245357", "input_tokens": 2882, "output_tokens": 64, "reasoning_tokens": 45, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "9e2f86cea68ab9c7345456c72e6826848ce0d80d90b08d55f36450276767981f", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 5.904899910092354, "dense": 22.989199962466955, "fusion": 0.12039998546242714, "generation": 489.9035000707954}, "wait_ms": 59396.99999978766, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q413", "type": "unanswerable", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["1706.03762:0022", "2501.12948:0081", "2309.07597:0030", "2309.07597:0029", "2309.07597:0021", "2309.07597:0036", "2309.07597:0032", "2309.07597:0031"], "text": "I couldn't find sufficient evidence in the available sources.", "abstained": true, "cited": [], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_420c059a6a", "input_tokens": 2979, "output_tokens": 37, "reasoning_tokens": 18, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "6d2d9b3822e8ad8922bebe4eff116f82633e3e97410a2d6996a1eba8038de754", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 8.269400103017688, "dense": 24.74610018543899, "fusion": 0.12989994138479233, "generation": 510.59220009483397}, "wait_ms": 60090.000000130385, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q502", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2203.11171:0009", "2203.11171:0046", "2203.11171:0008", "2203.11171:0002", "2203.11171:0006", "2203.11171:0025", "2203.11171:0005", "2203.11171:0012"], "text": "Weighting each sampled reasoning path by its probability does not substantially outperform a plain majority‑vote aggregation; the paper reports that an unweighted majority vote gives very similar accuracy to the normalized weighted‑sum method, and only the normalized weighting improves over an unnormalized version rather than over simple voting【1】.", "abstained": false, "cited": [1], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_fe269835c7", "input_tokens": 3135, "output_tokens": 139, "reasoning_tokens": 69, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "458ca8fc85ef1f83d8b58de65b0415dfa686217e5cb2b8c2a5e77ac24b1f3da8", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 10.810599895194173, "dense": 20.697100088000298, "fusion": 0.0838001724332571, "generation": 708.5926998406649}, "wait_ms": 60084.999999869615, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q503", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2205.11916:0024", "2205.11916:0018", "2205.11916:0016", "2205.11916:0027", "2205.11916:0011", "2205.11916:0019", "2205.11916:0004", "2205.11916:0017"], "text": "Zero‑shot‑CoT first concatenates the original question, the model‑generated reasoning sentence z, and a short answer‑trigger phrase (e.g., “Therefore, the answer (arabic numerals) is”) into a second prompt, then feeds this text to the language model to produce a short answer string [5]. After the model outputs that string, the “answer‑cleansing” step parses the first token that matches the required format—such as the first Arabic numeral for arithmetic problems or the first capital letter for multiple‑choice— and treats it as the final prediction [3].", "abstained": false, "cited": [5, 3], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_90620edd96", "input_tokens": 3028, "output_tokens": 152, "reasoning_tokens": 19, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "fb44ada714b46cbbd30da160c4726c3f5ba2e169384b4a4ee9f1f863bfe11c35", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 8.443000027909875, "dense": 26.13979997113347, "fusion": 0.09269989095628262, "generation": 1205.9096999000758}, "wait_ms": 60083.99999993853, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q505", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2302.04761:0046", "2302.04761:0047", "2302.04761:0007", "2302.04761:0041", "2302.04761:0034", "2302.04761:0052", "2302.04761:0006", "2302.04761:0005"], "text": "Toolformer keeps only those sampled API calls that (1) appear at positions where the model assigns a probability of generating the <API> token above a sampling threshold τₛ, and (2) whose execution reduces the loss (or perplexity) by at least a filtering threshold τ_f. Concretely, all positions i with pᵢ > τₛ are retained (up to the top k positions), and for each such position up to m calls are sampled; after execution, a call is kept only if the loss improvement L_i⁻ – L_i⁺ exceeds τ_f ([3][7]). In practice the authors use τₛ = 0.05 and τ_f = 1.0 for most tools (keeping the top k = 5 positions and sampling up to m = 5 calls), while for calculators and translators they relax the thresholds (τₛ = 0.0, k = 20, m = 10, τ_f = 0.5) to obtain enough calls ([2]).", "abstained": false, "cited": [3, 7, 2], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_c800245357", "input_tokens": 2090, "output_tokens": 288, "reasoning_tokens": 31, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "7764523a4ad9f4555282c8b805a77b4de7bd0ec0dc73d66fac11970962a0a658", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 6.976500153541565, "dense": 29.323299881070852, "fusion": 0.1517001073807478, "generation": 927.1845000330359}, "wait_ms": 0.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q506", "type": "factual", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2310.06825:0004", "2310.06825:0005", "2310.06825:0003", "2310.06825:0001", "2310.06825:0000", "2310.06825:0007", "2310.06825:0010", "2310.06825:0002"], "text": "Mistral 7B limits the KV cache by using a **rolling‑buffer cache**: the cache has a fixed size equal to the sliding‑window length \\(W\\) and stores the key/value pair for position \\(i\\) at slot \\(i \\bmod W\\). When the sequence index exceeds \\(W\\), older entries are overwritten, so the cache size no longer grows with the total number of tokens processed [1][2].  \nOn a 32 k‑token sequence this design cuts the cache‑memory requirement by roughly **8 ×** compared with a naïve growing cache [1][2].", "abstained": false, "cited": [1, 2], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_69dbc96c74", "input_tokens": 2793, "output_tokens": 200, "reasoning_tokens": 56, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "9485cc6b861d1932d7ee1de777b0d98cc5ad9da7474b03e76be80c3690c0b367", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 11.884599924087524, "dense": 28.75200007110834, "fusion": 0.12829992920160294, "generation": 849.9836998526007}, "wait_ms": 59161.99999991804, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
{"id": "q508", "type": "comparison", "setup": "hybrid", "chunk_ids": ["2205.11916:0024", "2205.11916:0008", "2205.11916:0007", "2205.11916:0003", "2205.11916:0000", "2205.11916:0018", "2501.12948:0146", "2205.11916:0027"], "text": "The original chain‑of‑thought (CoT) paper induces reasoning by providing few‑shot exemplars whose answers are written as step‑by‑step explanations, so the model sees a pattern of “think first, then answer” in the demonstrations【3】.  \nZero‑shot‑CoT achieves the same effect without any exemplars: it prepends a single, task‑agnostic template such as “Let’s think step by step” (or a similar phrase) to the input, prompting the model to generate a reasoning chain before producing the final answer【2】【4】.", "abstained": false, "cited": [3, 2, 4], "invalid_citations": [], "provider": "groq", "requested_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "system_fingerprint": "fp_8ea50c0161", "input_tokens": 2681, "output_tokens": 176, "reasoning_tokens": 47, "finish_reason": "stop", "cached": false, "request_hash": "2a74980b1b7418e24306a582768064a231e9c13afcdad04b86a3d2bbe6720d4e", "latency_ms": {"bm25": 11.89470011740923, "dense": 24.979199981316924, "fusion": 0.0909001100808382, "generation": 810.5930001474917}, "wait_ms": 0.0, "commit": "99d8e9995d80052b96156ab583735e6230772fa7"}
